---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PrincipleCard from '../components/PrincipleCard.astro';
import { byOrder } from '../lib/principles';

const principles = (await getCollection('principles')).sort(byOrder);
// SITE-01@v1: The hero leads with consistent decisions across contributors.
// SITE-02@v1: The comparison names decision drift as the costly failure.
// SITE-04@v1: Each contributor rebuilds judgment from current repository rules.
// SITE-05@v1: The page presents principles, routing, citations, and CLI checks as one system.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Principle Driven Development"
  description="Give developers and coding agents the same current principles for consistent decisions across a codebase."
>
  <section class="hero container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Principle Driven Development</span>
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1 class="display">Keep agent decisions <em>aligned with your codebase.</em></h1>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-side">
        <p class="lede"><strong>PDD is a repository system for consistent engineering decisions.</strong></p>
        <p>Memory and <code>AGENTS.md</code> files help, but they do not give every contributor the same judgment.</p>
        <p>PDD turns durable engineering judgment into versioned principles. It does not treat every repeated instruction as a principle.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="/blueprint">Set up PDD <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="button ghost" href="#how-it-works">How it works</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="decision-board" aria-label="How PDD prevents decision drift">
      <div class="board-head">
        <span>One codebase</span>
        <span class="live"><i></i> many contributors</span>
      </div>
      <div class="board-grid">
        <article class="board-column drift">
          <span class="board-label">Memory and instructions alone</span>
          <h2>Useful context.<br />Different judgment.</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Memory differs by person, agent, and session.</li>
            <li>Each handoff loses or changes context.</li>
            <li>Agents fill decision gaps in different ways.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="board-result"><span>Result</span> Reasonable choices drift apart.</p>
        </article>
        <div class="board-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
        <article class="board-column aligned">
          <span class="board-label">The PDD system</span>
          <h2>Current principles.<br />Shared judgment.</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Principles state how contributors must choose.</li>
            <li><code>AGENTS.md</code> routes contributors to each rule.</li>
            <li>Citations connect rules to code and reviews.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="board-result"><span>Result</span> Choices share one clear basis.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="board-note">PDD does not force one implementation. It gives each contributor the same basis for judgment.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="how-it-works" class="system container">
    <div class="system-head">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">A principle becomes a decision system.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="lede">A principle file is only documentation. PDD connects each rule to the agents, decisions, and code that rely on it.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="steps">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <div><h3>Find the judgment</h3><p>A repeated instruction is evidence, not a principle. Capture the reason that remains useful when the context changes.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <div><h3>Route every contributor</h3><p>List the token and summary in <code>AGENTS.md</code>. Link to the full rule.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <div><h3>Cite each dependency</h3><p>Add the versioned token where code, tests, comments, or reviews depend on the rule.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>04</span>
        <div><h3>Review rule changes</h3><p>When a rule changes, the CLI finds old citations that need review.</p></div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="system-outcome">
      <span>Outcome</span>
      <p>A new agent starts with the same current judgment, without memory from the previous agent.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/method">See the complete method <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="catalog">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="catalog-head">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Where principles come from</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">Start with examples. Add the principles your codebase earns.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="catalog-copy">
          <p>The public catalog contains general principles. Use only the rules that fit your codebase.</p>
          <p>Repeated problems and deliberate tradeoffs can reveal useful judgment. Adopt a principle only when that judgment must guide future decisions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="principle-sources">
        <article>
          <span>General principles</span>
          <h3>Useful across many codebases.</h3>
          <p>These rules cover recurring engineering and communication problems.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Codebase principles</span>
          <h3>Earned by one codebase.</h3>
          <p>These rules capture choices about your product, architecture, data, and risks.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="catalog-bar">
        <span>General examples</span>
        <a class="text-link" href="/principles">Browse all {principles.length} principles <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid">
        {principles.slice(0, 3).map((principle) => <PrincipleCard principle={principle} />)}
      </div>
      <div class="catalog-action">
        <p>Ready to add the judgment that matters in your codebase?</p>
        <a class="button primary" href="/blueprint">Use the blueprint <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: clamp(5rem, 9vw, 9rem); }
  .hero > .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.45fr) minmax(300px, 0.65fr); gap: 3rem 5rem; align-items: end; }
  .hero-copy .display { max-width: 860px; }
  .hero-side { display: grid; gap: 1rem; padding-bottom: 0.45rem; }
  .hero-side > p:not(.lede) { color: var(--muted); }
  .hero-side code { color: var(--ink); font-size: 0.9em; }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.7rem; margin-top: 0.8rem; }

  .decision-board { margin-top: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem); overflow: hidden; border-radius: 18px 18px 0 0; color: #eef3ee; background: var(--forest); box-shadow: 0 25px 70px rgba(23,63,49,0.18); }
  .board-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; padding: 1rem 1.3rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.14); font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.67rem; letter-spacing: 0.09em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .live { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; color: #b9c9bf; }
  .live i { width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--signal); box-shadow: 0 0 0 5px rgba(184,226,77,0.12); }
  .board-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr; gap: 1rem; align-items: stretch; padding: clamp(1.4rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .board-column { display: flex; min-width: 0; flex-direction: column; padding: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2.2rem); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.14); border-radius: 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.045); }
  .board-column.drift { opacity: 0.72; }
  .board-column.aligned { color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--signal); background: var(--signal); transform: rotate(-0.45deg); }
  .board-label { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.65rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .board-column h2 { margin-top: 1.6rem; font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.7rem); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -0.045em; line-height: 0.98; }
  .board-column ul { display: grid; gap: 0.7rem; margin: 2rem 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; color: inherit; }
  .board-column li { padding-left: 0.2rem; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .board-result { margin-top: auto; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid currentColor; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .board-result span { margin-right: 0.6rem; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.62rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .board-arrow { display: grid; place-items: center; color: var(--signal); font-size: 1.7rem; }
  .board-note { padding: 0 3rem 2rem; color: #b9c9bf; font-size: 0.86rem; text-align: center; }

  .system { padding: clamp(6rem, 11vw, 10rem) 0; }
  .system-head { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(280px, 0.65fr); gap: 3rem 5rem; align-items: end; }
  .system-head .eyebrow, .catalog-head .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .steps { margin-top: 5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .steps article { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0.25fr 1fr; padding: 1.7rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .steps article > span { color: var(--forest-light); font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.76rem; }
  .steps article > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1fr; gap: 2rem; }
  .steps h3 { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 2.5vw, 2.1rem); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -0.025em; }
  .steps p { color: var(--muted); }
  .system-outcome { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0.25fr 1fr auto; gap: 2rem; align-items: center; margin-top: 2rem; padding: 1.4rem; border-radius: 12px; color: var(--white); background: var(--forest); }
  .system-outcome > span { color: var(--signal); font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.66rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .system-outcome p { max-width: 650px; }
  .text-link { display: inline-flex; width: max-content; max-width: 100%; gap: 0.6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor; font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 750; }

  .catalog { padding: clamp(6rem, 11vw, 10rem) 0; background: var(--white); }
  .catalog-head { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.25fr) minmax(280px, 0.65fr); gap: 3rem 5rem; align-items: end; }
  .catalog-copy { display: grid; gap: 1rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .principle-sources { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 4rem; }
  .principle-sources article { padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 13px; background: var(--paper); }
  .principle-sources article:last-child { color: var(--white); background: var(--forest); }
  .principle-sources span, .catalog-bar > span { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.64rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .principle-sources article:last-child span { color: var(--signal); }
  .principle-sources h3 { margin-top: 1.8rem; font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3vw, 2.4rem); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
  .principle-sources p { margin-top: 0.6rem; color: inherit; font-size: 0.92rem; opacity: 0.75; }
  .catalog-bar { display: flex; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; gap: 2rem; margin-top: 5rem; padding-bottom: 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .card-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .catalog-action { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 2rem; margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .catalog-action p { color: var(--muted); }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .hero-grid, .system-head, .catalog-head { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .hero-side, .system-head .lede { max-width: 700px; }
    .card-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .system-outcome { grid-template-columns: 0.25fr 1fr; }
    .system-outcome .text-link { grid-column: 2; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 650px) {
    .board-grid, .principle-sources, .card-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .board-arrow { transform: rotate(90deg); }
    .board-column.aligned { transform: none; }
    .board-note { padding-inline: 1.4rem; }
    .steps article, .steps article > div, .system-outcome { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.8rem; }
    .steps article > span { margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
    .system-outcome .text-link { grid-column: auto; margin-top: 0.5rem; }
    .catalog-bar, .catalog-action { align-items: flex-start; flex-direction: column; }
  }
</style>
